{"id":"data-what-is-data","title":"Data science: what is data?","subject":"Data science","label":"Data science","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":182,"duration":181.63,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":483,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":12.235},{"id":"explain","title":"Raw to meaning","start":12.235,"end":39.235},{"id":"explain2","title":"Data types","start":39.235,"end":85.135},{"id":"example","title":"Class table","start":85.135,"end":116.685},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":116.685,"end":126.145},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":126.145,"end":133.335},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":133.335,"end":154.775},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":154.775,"end":181.63}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.17,"text":"Have you ever seen a list of numbers and still not known what it means?","w":[0.52,0.66,0.84,1.06,1.3,1.4,1.64,1.82,2.52,2.72,2.98,3.2,3.44,3.6,3.7]},{"s":0,"a":4.62,"b":9.87,"text":"I'm Kora. Data is everywhere, but raw facts only help when we turn them into meaning.","w":[4.72,4.92,5.72,6.2,6.46,7.24,7.48,7.78,8.28,8.54,8.78,8.92,9.04,9.24,9.38,9.58]},{"s":0,"a":10.17,"b":11.81,"text":"Today we'll see how that works.","w":[10.22,10.58,10.8,11.02,11.14,11.34]},{"s":1,"a":12.66,"b":18.71,"text":"Data means recorded facts. They can be numbers, words, measurements, clicks, or pictures.","w":[12.68,13.02,13.32,13.82,14.76,14.9,15.04,15.2,15.9,16.7,17.52,18,18.14]},{"s":1,"a":19.01,"b":25.81,"text":"On its own, data is raw. Organise it and find meaning, and it becomes information that helps a decision.","w":[19.12,19.24,19.46,20.12,20.48,20.66,21.62,22.12,22.3,22.48,22.8,23.48,23.62,23.7,24.14,24.82,25,25.3,25.38]},{"s":1,"a":26.11,"b":32.83,"text":"A dataset is a collection of data, most often a table. Each row is one record, like one student or one sale.","w":[26.16,26.26,26.88,27,27.08,27.54,27.66,28.28,28.6,28.9,28.98,29.7,29.96,30.3,30.5,30.7,31.24,31.5,31.66,32.18,32.38,32.58]},{"s":1,"a":33.13,"b":38.81,"text":"Each column is one variable, like name, age, or score. It holds one kind of fact for every record.","w":[33.18,33.42,33.82,34.02,34.14,34.64,34.92,35.34,35.56,35.7,36.5,36.62,37.02,37.2,37.44,37.56,37.88,38.16,38.4]},{"s":2,"a":39.66,"b":42.68,"text":"Quantitative data is numbers you can measure or count.","w":[39.72,40.36,40.82,41.02,41.36,41.5,41.66,42.14,42.28]},{"s":2,"a":42.98,"b":46.32,"text":"Discrete data is counted in whole steps, like number of siblings.","w":[42.98,43.46,43.84,43.98,44.34,44.48,44.74,45.12,45.38,45.64,45.76]},{"s":2,"a":46.62,"b":51.42,"text":"Continuous data is measured and can take any value in a range, like height or time.","w":[46.64,47.24,47.6,47.74,48.2,48.34,48.48,48.8,49,49.38,49.5,49.58,50.26,50.48,50.86,51.02]},{"s":2,"a":51.72,"b":58.6,"text":"Qualitative data, also called categorical data, is labels or groups, like blood group or favourite subject.","w":[51.76,52.38,53.12,53.46,53.76,54.42,54.9,55.16,55.7,55.88,56.68,56.94,57.24,57.62,57.76,58.08]},{"s":2,"a":58.9,"b":65.62,"text":"Nominal groups have no order, like colours. Ordinal groups have an order, like small, medium, large.","w":[58.98,59.38,59.72,59.94,60.22,60.78,61.02,62.04,62.4,62.9,63.1,63.28,63.78,64.08,64.76,65.16]},{"s":2,"a":65.92,"b":70.62,"text":"The type decides what you can do. You can average heights, but not favourite subjects.","w":[65.96,66.08,66.34,66.8,66.96,67.1,67.26,67.88,68,68.22,68.5,69.26,69.42,69.66,70.02]},{"s":2,"a":70.92,"b":74.19,"text":"For favourite subjects, you count how many are in each group.","w":[70.96,71.16,71.56,72.44,72.64,72.96,73.14,73.38,73.5,73.62,73.82]},{"s":2,"a":74.49,"b":84.71,"text":"Data comes from surveys, sensors, apps, receipts, and experiments. Data science asks a question, then collects, cleans and analyses data to answer it.","w":[74.52,74.88,75.18,75.44,76.28,77.24,77.74,78.34,78.46,79.64,79.98,80.54,80.84,80.92,81.42,81.68,82.48,82.88,83,83.68,84.02,84.22,84.54]},{"s":3,"a":85.56,"b":90.68,"text":"Take a class table with four columns: name, age, favourite subject, and test score.","w":[85.58,85.82,85.9,86.22,86.54,86.7,86.94,87.82,88.4,88.88,89.26,90,90.14,90.36]},{"s":3,"a":90.98,"b":95.33,"text":"Name is qualitative and nominal. Names are just labels with no order.","w":[91.08,91.36,91.52,92.26,92.42,93.44,93.82,93.94,94.2,94.62,94.82,95.08]},{"s":3,"a":95.63,"b":103.09,"text":"Age is quantitative and continuous, because it is measured and can take any value in a range. It can answer, what is the average age?","w":[95.76,96.02,96.2,96.96,97.12,98.18,98.44,98.54,98.7,99.16,99.26,99.42,99.72,99.94,100.36,100.46,100.54,101.24,101.32,101.52,101.9,102.12,102.22,102.44,102.76]},{"s":3,"a":103.54,"b":108.94,"text":"Favourite subject is qualitative and nominal. It can answer, which subject is most common?","w":[103.58,103.98,104.4,104.54,105.24,105.38,106.4,106.5,106.76,107.46,107.72,108.14,108.24,108.48]},{"s":3,"a":109.39,"b":116.26,"text":"Test score is quantitative and discrete, because marks are counted in whole steps. It can answer, what is the average score?","w":[109.42,109.7,110.08,110.22,110.8,110.92,111.92,112.22,112.5,112.62,113,113.14,113.36,114.36,114.44,114.66,115.2,115.36,115.46,115.62,115.92]},{"s":4,"a":117.11,"b":123.27,"text":"Quick check. Is the number of goals in a match discrete or continuous? And the time a runner takes?","w":[117.18,117.5,118.22,118.32,118.48,118.76,118.9,119.36,119.46,119.56,120.02,120.66,120.8,121.86,121.98,122.12,122.44,122.54,122.8]},{"s":4,"a":123.72,"b":125.72,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[123.74,124.08,124.34,124.46,124.74,125.2,125.38]},{"s":5,"a":126.57,"b":132.91,"text":"Goals are discrete because you count them in whole steps, and time is continuous because it can take any value in a range.","w":[126.62,127.04,127.18,127.76,128.04,128.2,128.46,128.62,128.72,128.94,129.82,129.98,130.3,130.42,131.02,131.3,131.38,131.54,131.82,132.02,132.38,132.48,132.56]},{"s":6,"a":133.76,"b":141.44,"text":"First, do not treat code numbers like phone numbers or jersey numbers as quantities. They are labels, so count them or group them instead.","w":[133.86,134.54,134.68,134.9,135.18,135.48,135.8,136.02,136.28,136.64,136.8,137.16,137.48,137.62,138.54,138.72,138.86,139.76,139.96,140.24,140.46,140.62,140.86,141.04]},{"s":6,"a":141.74,"b":147.27,"text":"Second, never average categories. For favourite subjects, count how many are in each group.","w":[141.86,142.58,142.98,143.28,144.38,144.56,144.92,145.66,145.96,146.16,146.46,146.6,146.74,146.94]},{"s":6,"a":147.57,"b":154.35,"text":"Third, always keep units, and remember that good data beats more data. Check that your data is accurate and relevant.","w":[147.58,148.14,148.5,148.82,149.36,149.48,149.92,150.14,150.38,150.78,151.1,151.32,152.12,152.38,152.5,152.7,153.06,153.28,153.72,153.86]},{"s":7,"a":155.2,"b":161.08,"text":"Recap. Data is recorded facts. Organised data becomes information for decisions.","w":[155.28,156.24,156.74,156.88,157.42,158.56,159.02,159.34,159.72,160.32,160.46]},{"s":7,"a":161.38,"b":166.38,"text":"A dataset is a table of records and variables. Data types decide what you can do.","w":[161.44,161.54,162.2,162.32,162.42,162.76,162.9,163.32,163.44,164.54,164.9,165.28,165.72,165.86,165.98,166.14]},{"s":7,"a":166.68,"b":172.12,"text":"Quantitative data is discrete or continuous. Qualitative data is nominal or ordinal.","w":[166.7,167.34,167.78,167.9,168.56,168.68,169.82,170.4,170.8,171.02,171.6,171.8]},{"s":7,"a":172.42,"b":176.52,"text":"Top tip: always ask what each column means before you calculate.","w":[172.48,172.78,173.54,174.04,174.26,174.48,174.72,175.12,175.44,175.78,175.92]},{"s":7,"a":176.82,"b":181.03,"text":"Knowzone helps you practise these ideas step by step, until they feel simple.","w":[176.9,177.38,177.6,177.78,178.22,178.46,178.86,179.12,179.32,180.02,180.28,180.42,180.66]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"A list of numbers can still be unclear"},{"at":4.52,"kind":"term","text":"Data","detail":"Raw facts; need meaning"},{"at":10.07,"kind":"text","text":"Today: raw facts → meaning"}]},{"at":12.41,"heading":"Raw to meaning","items":[{"at":12.56,"kind":"term","text":"Data","detail":"Recorded facts: numbers, words, measurements, clicks, pictures"},{"at":18.91,"kind":"term","text":"Information","detail":"Organised data with meaning; helps a decision"},{"at":26.01,"kind":"term","text":"Dataset","detail":"Collection of data, often a table; row = one record"},{"at":33.03,"kind":"term","text":"Variable","detail":"Column; one kind of fact for every record"}]},{"at":39.41,"heading":"Data types","items":[{"at":39.56,"kind":"term","text":"Quantitative","detail":"Numbers you can measure or count"},{"at":42.88,"kind":"term","text":"Discrete","detail":"Counted in whole steps, e.g. siblings"},{"at":46.52,"kind":"term","text":"Continuous","detail":"Measured; any value in a range, e.g. height, time"},{"at":51.62,"kind":"term","text":"Qualitative","detail":"Labels or groups, e.g. blood group, subject"},{"at":58.8,"kind":"term","text":"Nominal / ordinal","detail":"Nominal: no order (colours); ordinal: order (S, M, L)"}]},{"at":65.67,"heading":"Type decides use","items":[{"at":65.82,"kind":"text","text":"Type decides what you can do"},{"at":70.82,"kind":"text","text":"For subjects, count each group"},{"at":74.39,"kind":"term","text":"Data science","detail":"Ask; collect, clean, analyse data to answer"},{"at":74.39,"kind":"text","text":"Sources: surveys, sensors, apps, receipts, experiments"}]},{"at":85.31,"heading":"Class table","items":[{"at":85.46,"kind":"text","text":"Columns: name, age, subject, score"},{"at":90.88,"kind":"term","text":"Name","detail":"Qualitative, nominal: labels, no order"},{"at":95.53,"kind":"term","text":"Age","detail":"Quantitative, continuous; average age"},{"at":103.44,"kind":"term","text":"Favourite subject","detail":"Qualitative, nominal; most common subject"},{"at":109.29,"kind":"term","text":"Test score","detail":"Quantitative, discrete: whole steps; average score"}]},{"at":116.69,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":116.69,"kind":"question","text":"Is the number of goals in a match discrete or continuous? And the time a runner takes?"}]},{"at":126.32,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":126.47,"kind":"term","text":"Goals","detail":"Discrete: counted in whole steps"},{"at":126.47,"kind":"term","text":"Time","detail":"Continuous: any value in a range"}]},{"at":133.51,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":133.66,"kind":"wrong","text":"Treat phone/jersey numbers as quantities"},{"at":133.66,"kind":"right","text":"They are labels: count or group them"},{"at":141.64,"kind":"wrong","text":"Average categories like favourite subjects"},{"at":141.64,"kind":"right","text":"Count how many are in each group"},{"at":147.47,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ignore units; more data is always better"}]},{"at":154.95,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":155.1,"kind":"text","text":"Data = recorded facts; organised → information"},{"at":161.28,"kind":"text","text":"Dataset = records × variables; types decide use"},{"at":166.58,"kind":"text","text":"Quant: discrete/continuous; qual: nominal/ordinal"},{"at":172.32,"kind":"tip","text":"Ask what each column means before you calculate"},{"at":176.72,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: practise step by step"}]}],"check":{"at":125.97,"seconds":10,"question":"Is the number of goals in a match discrete or continuous? And the time a runner takes?","answer":"Goals: discrete (counted in whole steps). Time: continuous (any value in a range)."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}